-- title:
--   Geometric fibre at ℓ≠ p of the j-chart of X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 0$ and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $\ell$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ is a non-unit of $A$, and assume that the residue field $k=$ `ResidueField ↥A` has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed; $k$ and the quotient ring $\mathrm{Afin}\,p/(\ell)$ are both given $\mathbf Z/\ell$-algebra structures, where $\mathrm{Afin}\,p$ denotes the finite-$j$ chart subalgebra `chartAlgFin ℤ` of the modular function field $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` $\subset\mathbf Q(\!(q)\!)$ (the intermediate field of $\mathbf Q$ generated by the divisor expansions of level $p$) attached over $\mathbf Z$ to the single element `IgusaScheme.jFull p` $=j$, and $(\ell)$ is the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $\ell$. The assertion is the existence of a $k$-algebra isomorphism
--   $$e\colon k\otimes_{\mathbf Z/\ell}\bigl(\mathrm{Afin}\,p/(\ell)\bigr)\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathrm{chartRing}_k\bigl(\{\bar j\}\bigr),$$
--   where the target is, by the definition of `CurveModel.chartRing`, the subalgebra of elements of `modularFunctionFieldFullC k p` $\subset k(\!(q)\!)$ integral over $k[\bar j]$, with $\bar j=$ `jqModC k` the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image of the power series `jNum` under $\mathbf Z\to k$, together with its membership in that field; and $e$ satisfies the normalisation that the underlying Laurent series of $e\bigl(1\otimes(j\bmod \ell)\bigr)$, with $j\bmod\ell$ the class of `jChartFin ℤ F (jFull p)`, is $\bar j$.
--
--   This is Igusa's good reduction of $X_0(p)$ at a prime $\ell\neq p$, expressed in the currency of chart rings for the model over $\mathbf Z$: the geometric fibre at $\ell$ of the finite-$j$ chart is the integral closure of $\bar k[\bar j]$ in the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field of level $p$, compatibly with $j$. It is obtained from the corresponding statement over $\mathbf Z_{(\ell)}$ together with the base-change description of chart algebras along a localisation, and it feeds the étaleness statement `exists_forall_etale_zmod_tensorProduct_quotient_span_aeval_jChartFin`.
-- source:
